{"kind":"stack","id":"skeleton-muscles","title":"Skeletons and muscles","theme":{"background":"#f4f9ff","foreground":"#1d2b3a","font":"Comic Sans MS, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Skeleton"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"The hard frame inside a body. It gives shape, protects organs and helps us move."}],"actions":[],"buttons":[{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Muscle"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"Soft tissue that pulls on bones to make them move. Muscles can only pull, not push."}],"actions":[],"buttons":[{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which part of the body protects the brain?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"The skull","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}],"why":"Category: a part of the skeleton. The skull is the bone case that protects the brain."},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"The ribs","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}],"why":"Pupils confuse the ribs with the skull because both are bones, but the ribs protect the heart and lungs."},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"The spine","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}],"why":"Pupils mix up the spine with the skull, but the spine protects the spinal cord."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"Which of these animals has a skeleton inside its body?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"A dog","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}],"why":"Category: a vertebrate animal. Dogs have a bony skeleton inside the body."},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"A snail","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}],"why":"Pupils think a snail's shell is a skeleton, but it is an outside cover, not a bony frame."},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"A worm","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}],"why":"Pupils assume soft-bodied animals have no support, but a worm supports itself with fluid pressure, not bones."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"What do muscles do?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Pull on bones to make them move","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}],"why":"Category: a job of body parts. Muscles contract and pull on bones to create movement."},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Store food for the body","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}],"why":"Pupils mix up muscles with fat, which stores energy."},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"Carry oxygen around the body","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}],"why":"Pupils mix up muscles with blood, which carries oxygen."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"You are out walking and you trip on a step. Your arm goes out to save you. What do you do next?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Check your arm is OK","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Keep walking as if nothing happened","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"You check your arm. Your bones are safe because your skeleton holds your arm steady. Well done for taking care of yourself."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"You keep walking, but your sore arm shows that your muscles were strained. Rest it and it will feel better."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which animal has muscles and a skeleton to help it move?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"A horse","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}],"why":"Category: an animal with a skeleton. Horses have a bony skeleton and muscles that pull on it."},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"A jellyfish","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}],"why":"Pupils think jellyfish move like animals with bones, but they have no skeleton."},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"A sponge","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}],"why":"Pupils assume all animals have muscles and bones, but sponges have neither."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Why do we have a skeleton?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"To give shape and protect organs","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}],"why":"Category: a job of the skeleton. It gives shape and protects soft organs inside the body."},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"To make food inside the body","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}],"why":"Pupils mix up the skeleton with the stomach, which digests food."},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"To send messages to the brain","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}],"why":"Pupils mix up the skeleton with the nerves, which carry messages."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Well done! You finished the skeletons and muscles lesson."},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"You now know how skeletons and muscles help us support, protect and move."}],"actions":[]}}
